  "rederived": "0.7.2 (2026-10-14): DestroyTreasureCondition and OpenTreasureContainer removed, their classes deleted with the treasure-map objective (42 types remain). ShowEventTitle re-read whole from the 0.7.2 source: 9 keys, `Style` added after SecondaryTitle, `IsMajor` kept but now Validators.deprecated() and mapped onto style; required set unchanged. The other 42 reproduce unchanged.",
  "requiredness": "Re-derived by hand from the decompiled 0.7.2 source; the old single `required` list was the union of two different facts. `null_validated`: the field's validator chain holds an instance of NonNullValidator (the only thing that makes an omitted key fail; measured by maintenance/probes/requiredness/run.sh). `strict_null`: a `true` third KeyedCodec argument (never makes an omitted key fail). Every kept key cites the line it was read on. `required_from_key_table` is what the docs' key tables claimed and is NOT a measurement."
